Verification: 26 frontend tests, 27 domain/architecture tests, solution build with zero warnings/errors, frontend/Docker builds, and Edge at 320/360/390/640/768/1280px passed. Browser checks cover reflow, table semantics, target sizes, keyboard/focus, RTL editor/preview/viewer, real CAPTCHA-backed reply, localization/error/draft handling, depth15 and failure/recovery. All 18 paging scenarios passed on the retained million-comment corpus; original rows/schema/history of all three DBs, volumes, environment and checkpoint hashes were preserved. Other backend suites were unchanged and not rerun; the previous 235-test full run belongs to 1.1.0.12. Manual screen-reader and VS/Workbench GUI checks were not performed. Next: 1.1.0.14 SecurityReview.

## 1.1.0.12 FileViewer — 2026-10-30

`CommentsService/v_1.1.0.12_FileViewer`

FileViewer (1.1.0.12): click an image or TXT filename to open a modal with fade/scale effects. Previous/Next and Left/Right cycle through attachments in currently visible comments, including expanded replies; hidden/unloaded replies and other pages are not fetched. Escape, Close viewer or the backdrop closes it. Focus stays inside and returns to the opener; background scrolling is locked. Reduced-motion preferences disable animations. Downloads preserve the stored normalized PNG or the original TXT bytes, using generated UUID filenames. TXT is decoded as strict UTF-8 and rendered as literal text, never HTML; a leading BOM is not displayed. Loading, failure and Retry states preserve the comment draft. Requests are bounded and canceled on navigation/close; temporary image URLs are revoked.

`GET /api/images/{id}?download=true` adds attachment disposition; without it the existing inline PNG route is unchanged. TXT continues to use `/api/text-files/{id}` with its safe headers and exact bytes. FileClient separates the viewer from HTTP; backend Domain/Application/Infrastructure boundaries and Onion/OOP/SOLID remain intact. No new dependency or migration. Upgrade 1.1.0.11 → 1.1.0.12 by rebuilding/restarting the app with the same environment, Compose overrides and volumes; retain existing databases and verified checkpoints. Latest migration remains `20261030130243_TextAttachments`.

Validation for 1.1.0.12: 235 backend tests (27/84/56/68), 23 frontend tests, frontend/Docker builds and Edge desktop/360px passed. Browser coverage includes real CAPTCHA-backed image/TXT/reply fixtures, 100 KiB, literal Unicode/HTML, exact downloads, arrows/wrap, close paths, focus, draft retention, 404/503/retry, stale requests, URL cleanup, EN/RU/UA, reduced motion and reload. All 18 paging scenarios passed on the retained million-comment corpus without reseeding. All three databases, volumes and checkpoint hashes were preserved. No migration/restore rehearsal was needed for this code-only change. VS/Workbench GUI was not checked. Next: 1.1.0.13 ResponsiveUi.

## 1.1.0.11 TextAttachments — 2026-10-30

`CommentsService/v_1.1.0.11_TextAttachments`

TXT attachments (1.1.0.11): roots and replies accept one optional attachment: an image OR a `.txt` file. TXT must contain 1..102400 bytes (100 KiB), strict UTF-8; BOM, Unicode, CR/LF and tabs are preserved byte-for-byte. Invalid encoding and control characters other than CR/LF/tab are rejected; HTML/script text is accepted as literal text. Filename/MIME do not establish content validity. Multipart uses `textFile` with the usual comment/CAPTCHA fields; never send both file parts. JSON text-only creation remains available. Invalid TXT returns 400/errors.textFile. CAPTCHA is consumed before content processing; retry with a fresh code. The localized picker keeps draft/file on errors, clears on success and permits removing/replacing a selection.

DTOs add nullable `textFile: {id,fileName,sizeBytes}`; list/page/reply projections omit file bytes. `GET /api/text-files/{id}` downloads exact bytes as `text/plain; charset=utf-8`, generated UUID `.txt` filename, attachment disposition, nosniff, no-store and sandbox CSP; missing files return 404. HTML is never rendered. Full viewer/effects remain 1.1.0.12 FileViewer.

Upgrade 1.1.0.10 → 1.1.0.11: stop all writers, restore-verify a current checkpoint (include the benchmark when present), build, explicitly migrate every used database, then restart using the existing volumes. Migration `20261030130243_TextAttachments` adds TextAttachments: Id, unique CommentId FK CASCADE, sanitized FileName varchar128, SizeBytes, Data bytea; checks enforce 1..102400 bytes and matching size. Existing authors/comments/images and migration IDs are preserved. Down refuses while TXT rows exist. Bytes and comment are committed atomically in the same PostgreSQL database/backup; no filesystem volume. Preserve verified pre-upgrade copies, accounting for changes after their checkpoint.

Onion: Domain enforces immutable ownership/defensive bytes and one attachment per comment; Application defines processing/read ports and coordinates the transaction; Infrastructure validates UTF-8 and implements EF storage/queries; API binds streams and sets download headers. No new external dependency.

Validation: 235 backend tests (27 Domain,84 Application,56 Infrastructure/database,68 HTTP),16 frontend tests, frontend/Docker builds, restore upgrade/downgrade round trip and populated-TXT downgrade guard passed. Edge desktop/360px passed real CAPTCHA, TXT root/reply, boundary size, exact Unicode/BOM/CRLF/HTML download, restart persistence, safe headers, rejection/draft retention/removal, exclusive selection and EN/RU/UA without JavaScript errors. All 18 retained-million-corpus paging scenarios passed without reseeding; original row fingerprints, metadata, volumes and restore-verified checkpoints were retained. GUI import in VS/Workbench is not checked.


## 1.1.0.10 ImageAttachments — 2026-10-30

Branch: `CommentsService/v_1.1.0.10_ImageAttachments`

- Added one optional image to root/reply creation through multipart/form-data while preserving JSON text-only writes and required CAPTCHA. Domain image invariants/defensive bytes, Application processing/read ports and transactional graph creation, Infrastructure codec/EF adapters and thin HTTP boundaries preserve Onion/OOP/SOLID.
- Accepts JPG/JPEG, GIF and PNG after matching extension/actual codec and complete decode. Applies EXIF orientation, proportionally fits within 320×240 without upscaling/cropping, retains transparency and re-encodes PNG without original metadata/trailing bytes. Animated GIF uses its first frame. Bounds: source 5 MiB,16M pixels,10000/side; two decoder slots; normalized payload max512 KiB. SkiaSharp4.154.0/Linux assets and upstream notices are included.
- Stores image bytes/metadata in the same PostgreSQL transaction/volumes as the comment; no orphan filesystem files or extra volume. GET /api/images/{id} serves canonical inline PNG with nosniff. Public comment projections include nullable image metadata, never payload bytes. Added file picker/remove, localized errors, draft/file retention, reset on success and thumbnails; full viewer remains planned.
- Migration 20261030122207_ImageAttachments adds only its table, unique CommentId/index, bounds and cascading owner FK; prior comment/author fields and root/reply relationships remain intact. All three persistent DBs were upgraded after current pre-upgrade dumps were restore/fingerprint verified, including paging-v1. An owned restore passed upgrade/empty-image downgrade round trip; downgrade with images is blocked atomically. Previous recovery points were replaced only after successful verification.
- Passed 208 backend tests (26 domain/architecture,81 application,39 infrastructure/database,62 HTTP),14 frontend tests and frontend/Docker builds. Application was rerun after adding two image-graph tests; final81 pass. Tests cover formats, dimensions, EXIF, alpha/first-frame GIF, corrupt/truncated/spoofed/oversized input, domain ownership/byte isolation, atomic storage/read/cascade, multipart field rules and safe delivery.
- Edge desktop/360px passed real CAPTCHA + multipart JPG/GIF/PNG, images on roots/replies, metadata/thumbnail/read/reload and identical image bytes after restarting the owned app. Rejected invalid contents/extension and oversized body; kept draft/file on errors, removed selection correctly, EN/RU/UA, no JS errors. Only owned fixtures/container were removed.
- The retained million-corpus rows/metadata matched full aggregate fingerprints; only the new migration history entry changed. All18 paging benchmark cases passed on the same corpus after upgrade, without reseeding. Verified pre-upgrade checkpoints/volumes retained; paused independent preview restarted with its original image. Documentation/schema/Workbench projection updated EN/RU/UA; VS/Workbench GUI not checked. Next:1.1.0.11 TextAttachments.

## 1.1.0.9 Captcha — 2026-10-30

Branch: `CommentsService/v_1.1.0.9_Captcha`

- Added required CAPTCHA for root/reply creation through segregated Application issuer/verifier ports. Verification precedes parent lookup/staged writes; PNG rendering and a bounded concurrent hash store are Infrastructure adapters. No production bypass, external graphics package or database migration.
- GET /api/captcha returns only id, PNG data URL and UTC expiry with no-store headers. Six secure-random Latin letters/digits are case-insensitive, expire after five minutes, and are consumed atomically by any verification attempt. Refresh invalidates the replaced ID; 2,048-slot capacity/expiry cleanup bounds memory and full capacity returns 429. Process restart invalidates outstanding challenges.
- Added localized image/code/refresh controls, required-input checks, expired/loading/unavailable submit protection, request cancellation and automatic challenge renewal after POST attempts. Errors preserve the draft; read/preview endpoints remain CAPTCHA-free.
- Passed 182 backend tests (22 domain/architecture, 79 application, 26 infrastructure/database, 55 HTTP) and 13 frontend tests, frontend/Docker builds. Verified exact expiry/restart, wrong/replaced/spent IDs, case-insensitive success, 64-way atomic consumption, capacity recovery, PNG structure, no response answer metadata and rejected writes without new rows. Existing unrelated use-case suites use explicit test-only verifier doubles; the real HTTP flow exercises the production store/renderer.
- Edge desktop/360 px passed real raster input, required/wrong/refresh/spent/success/replay, protected root/reply, double-click protection, code renewal, draft retention, image outage/expiry and EN/RU/UA without JS errors. Test-only image reading used real pixels, not a debug/answer endpoint. Owned fixtures/container were removed.
- Dev/test data/schema/history, persistent volume identity, original checkpoint hashes and million-corpus full-row fingerprints/metadata stayed unchanged. Documentation updated EN/RU/UA; VS/Workbench GUI not checked. Next: 1.1.0.10 ImageAttachments.

## 1.1.0.8 SortingPagination — 2026-10-30

Branch: `CommentsService/v_1.1.0.8_SortingPagination`

- Added GetRootPage in Application, typed sort queries in its persistence port and an Infrastructure repeatable-read count/items projection. GET /api/comments/page supports userName/email/createdAt asc/desc, fixed 25-root pages, totals and deterministic UUID ties. Default is LIFO; replies are excluded from root counts. Legacy bounded latest-array/reply routes remain compatible. No application schema migration.
- Added sort/direction controls, First/Previous/Next/Last, page jump, URL/reload persistence, stale-bookmark correction, localized labels and retained drafts/results on failure. New roots return to newest-first page one; replies retain the current page. Onion/OOP/SOLID boundaries remain intact.
- Passed 174 backend tests (22 domain/architecture, 78 application, 20 database, 54 HTTP), 12 frontend tests and frontend/Docker builds. Tests cover six sorts, equal-value boundaries, no duplicates/lost roots, reply exclusion, invalid/injection-like parameters and cancellation.
- Edge desktop/360 px passed a real 55-root fixture, 25/25/last pages, page jump/reload URLs, all six sorts, replies on page two, new-root reset, draft/error retention, empty/stale/invalid bookmarks and EN/RU/UA without JS errors. Owned browser rows/container were removed; working/test data/schema/history baselines, volume identity and original checkpoint hashes matched.
- Prepared persistent paging-v1 once in the separate comments_benchmark DB: 1,000,000 comments, 800,000 roots, 200,000 replies, 10,000 authors and 32,000 pages. Repeated preparation reused its version/count without data writes; full-row aggregate fingerprints and metadata matched across reuse/measurements. Functional test data stays separate.
- Measured 18 sort/direction/page cases with three samples, then validated the portable temporary-API CLI in a second run on the same corpus. First-page medians 51.93–323.61 ms; deep name/email medians 1338.42–1821.36 ms. These local observations are documented with OFFSET/join cost, not presented as an SLA. No speculative index migration/cache was introduced.
- Added opt-in benchmark migration/check and checkpoint coverage. A temporary checkpoint restored and fingerprint-verified all three DBs including the million-row corpus; only its six owned probe artifacts/restore DBs were removed. Existing recovery points remain unchanged. Documentation and benchmark procedures are EN/RU/UA. VS/Workbench GUI not checked. Next: 1.1.0.9 Captcha.

## 1.1.0.7 CommentThreads — 2026-10-30

Branch: `CommentsService/v_1.1.0.7_CommentThreads`

- Added immutable parent/root relationships and reply creation for any existing comment without an application depth limit. Missing parents are rejected before staging author/comment; rootId is derived by Domain and cannot be supplied by HTTP clients.
- Added GetReplies in Application and bounded, no-tracking cursor queries in Infrastructure. Latest list contains roots only; direct replies use descending UTC time/UUID, 25 by default and 100 maximum. Invalid/foreign cursors are rejected. Onion/OOP/SOLID boundaries remain intact.
- Added Reply/Cancel, recipient indication, lazy Show/Hide/More replies, branch retry and refresh, draft retention and EN/RU/UA messages. Iterative rendering has no thread depth cap; visual indentation is capped, with the actual level displayed.
- Added migration 20261030101720_CommentThreads: ParentId nullable, RootId backfilled from each old Id, composite parent/root RESTRICT foreign key, alternate key, check and indexes. All previous fields/rows survived upgrades of both persistent databases. Current pre-upgrade checkpoints replaced older candidates only after successful restore/fingerprint verification.
- Rehearsed upgrade and roots-only downgrade on an owned restore: data/schema/history round trip passed; downgrade with replies was refused atomically. Only the owned restore was removed; checkpoint hashes and persistent volumes were retained.
- Passed 150 backend tests (22 domain/architecture, 68 application, 14 database, 46 HTTP), 10 frontend tests, frontend/Docker builds and runtime readiness. Unit tests cover depth 1000; HTTP/PostgreSQL cover 40 levels, keyset ties, root isolation, invalid parents and restricted deletion.
- Edge desktop/360 px passed real root/reply/nested XHTML create/read/reload, hide/show, cancel/draft/missing-target, 27 siblings as 25+2, live refresh, read failure/retry, EN/RU/UA and a read-only 60-level rendering fixture without JS errors. Owned browser rows were removed leaf-first; migrated data/schema/history baselines, volumes and checkpoint hashes matched afterward. VS/Workbench GUI was not checked. Next: 1.1.0.8 SortingPagination.

